  "title": "Surprisal as negative log evidence",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "8d04100d-d403-4c75-b0a7-5ef8bcbefaeb",
      "text": "Surprisal is the self-information of a state: how improbable it is under the density that characterizes the thing. In Bayesian terms it is the negative log model evidence, so lowering surprisal is gathering evidence for oneself.",
